⚠️ **IMPORTANT: This real-repo-state test makes the root `dart test` suite host-state dependent — red on macOS dev checkouts after any Flutter build**

The test runs the gate against the *working tree* (`Process.runSync('bash', [scriptPath, appMin])`, default repo root). On a macOS dev machine, Flutter 3.47 ships SwiftPM enabled-by-default and migrates the clone at build time (the exact mechanism this PR documents): after any local `flutter build`/`run`:

- `flutter_app/macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` carries the `FlutterGeneratedPluginSwiftPackage` marker (a tracked-file mutation), and/or
- `flutter_app/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/Packages/` exists (gitignored, so invisible in `git status`).

Either condition fails this test with the gate's lane-remediation error — so the PR description's own note ("dev machines with default SwiftPM unaffected") does not hold for macOS contributors running the suite (incl. the pre-commit fast gate). CI is unaffected (root `dart test` runs on Linux only), which is why this is not blocking.

Suggested hardening (pick one):

```dart
test('the committed tree passes the gate (real repo state)', () {
  if (Directory('flutter_app/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/Packages').existsSync() ||
      File('flutter_app/macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj')
          .readAsStringSync()
          .contains('FlutterGeneratedPluginSwiftPackage')) {
    // A local SwiftPM-enabled build migrated this checkout; the committed
    // state is what the lane pins — assert that instead of the live tree.
  }
  ...
});
```

- or assert the *committed* shape via `git show HEAD:flutter_app/macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` instead of the file on disk;
- or `@Tags(['io'])`-style scope it to CI hosts per the repo's existing tag conventions.

